module gunbc.plans.logical_work_realization

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import std.types { List }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock, CodeBlock }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { h2, p, li, ul, ol }
import gunbc.design_ruling { project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts }

fn logical_work_realization_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    p(text: "Proposal for review. Give ordinary callers a small logical interface for reads, writes and computations, with deployment-scoped SLO and arbitration defaults. This plan specifies the first consumer and the conditions for implementation; it does not implement implicit operand completion, change runtime policy, or authorize a deployment."),
    h2(text: "1. The consumer problem and intended interface"),
    p(text: "A caller should express the work and its irreducible inputs. Storage delegates to the existing fabric storage interface: fabric owns backend selection, placement and the selected backend's prerequisites. Worktree claims consume that interface rather than introducing a file-versus-network chooser of their own. The broader direction includes compute placement and reuse. Correctness requirements constrain admissible realizations; cost and service-level objectives guide the choice within those constraints. The first implementation should establish the interface and move consumers onto it using simple configured inputs, without waiting for production metering."),
    CodeBlock { code: "// Desired consumer surface; illustrative, not implemented inference.\nworktree_claim_record_before_add(claim: claim)" },
    p(text: "The example proposes a replacement of the existing worktree_claim_record_before_add(root: NonEmptyStr, claim: WorktreeClaim) signature: root becomes a supplied realization dependency. It is not a second operation with the same name. Cut over the production consumer gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate and test.claim.roadmap.attempt_worktree_claim_wet_witness, along with the settlement entry points in the inventory."),
    p(text: "The operation and existing logical identity determine the requested resource; repeated use addresses the same authority under its existing semantics. The logical effects remain represented: pure computations, observed reads, durable mutations and fresh effects retain their own identity, freshness, ordering and retry contracts. The common completion path does not make a mutation memoizable."),
    h2(text: "2. One small policy surface"),
    p(text: "Ordinary calls inherit a scoped service/deployment profile. The optional surface has two concepts: SLO requirements and arbitration policy. A profile is a reference to their existing authorities, not a copy of owner, path, credentials, provider facts or per-operation knobs. Each inherited requirement must resolve to its owning declaration, cited by module and symbol; delivery 1 names those declarations. A required value with no such authority remains unresolved. An explicit declaration that the root adds no performance target is distinct from failing to find a required target. An explicit departure is stated at the scope that owns the requirement and cannot weaken the operation's mandatory contract."),
    CodeBlock { code: "// Conceptual fabric-owned policy; not new .dag syntax or a new policy algebra.\nrealization_profile {\n  slo: inherit_service_requirements,\n  arbitration: configured_file_and_r2_example,\n}\n\n// Explicit example inputs for one fixed object put/readback workload:\n// backend       cost (micro-USD/operation)   latency (ms/operation)\n// local files   0                            0\n// R2            1                            1\n// These are supplied example predictions, not provider prices or measurements." },
    p(text: "The example deliberately supplies local cost/latency as 0/0 and R2 as positive values so local wins when both are admissible. Zero is an explicit example assumption, never a substitution for an unknown reading. The values carry their example/predicted standing into the SelectionReceipt evidence snapshot. Reuse std.realization_schedule::CostAxisPredicted and CostTimePredicted where those carriers fit, and extdeps.external_authority::CitedFigureStanding for an external figure's grounding; do not mint a measured receipt for supplied numbers. Replacing them with calibrated or metered inputs is a different decision through the same interface. An example prediction cannot establish a declared physical SLO floor."),
    p(text: "SLO means a named requirement with a subject, operation/workload, metric and units, bound, observation scope/window, evidence rule and consequence. A latency percentile without a population/window is incomplete. Existing requirements are inherited; this proposal invents no universal millisecond, availability or currency target. Cost objectives include the modeled costs of realizing and operating the choice, including setup, transfer and migration where applicable; an unknown cost is never zero."),
    h2(text: "3. Initial defaults and their limits"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "Contract: inherit the operation's existing consistency, durability, retention, sharing, access and effect requirements. Performance preferences do not weaken them. Worktree claims additionally require enumeration for recovery and continuity of their authority."),
      li(text: "SLO: inherit established service/deployment requirements. If no additional performance target is declared, make no additional performance promise. A required but unknown bound or observation remains unresolved; it is not the same as no extra bound."),
      li(text: "Arbitration: fabric storage owns the local-file and R2 candidates and their configured example readings. Use those inputs immediately to exercise selection and adopt the interface. For already allocated mutable state, preserve its existing authority; an isolated fresh resource can exercise a different admitted backend without silently relocating live state."),
      li(text: "Selection: fabric consumes std.decision::select_realization and its SelectionReceipt, with std.pareto and the existing ValuedObjective machinery. UniqueSurvivorRequired handles a unique survivor; PreferSurvivor only selects a feasible survivor. No feature-specific scoring or list-order preference."),
      li(text: "Evidence: supplied example predictions can drive the pilot's choice under its declared policy. Required SLO floors still need their own admissible evidence and consequence; missing such evidence returns SelectionNeedsEvidence. Two surviving alternatives without an applicable policy return SelectionNeedsPolicy. Production metering is a later refinement, not an interface-adoption prerequisite."),
      li(text: "Prerequisites: use the selected realization's existing ensure, observation and authorization routes under the responsible root's authority. Correct existing state is Noop. Missing authority is never manufactured by the constructor."),
      li(text: "Continuity: keep a mutable resource's identity across calls and restarts. An unavailable authoritative store refuses; it does not become an empty local store. Moving existing state is a separately admitted transition whose correctness and cost are part of the decision."),
    ]),
    p(text: "The two-backend example must execute both choices. In the first isolated context, both are admissible and local wins on the supplied inputs. In the second, a declared sharing/reachability requirement excludes the host-local candidate before ranking, so R2 wins if it meets that requirement. Name the actual candidate scope: fabric's served file backend can also be shared, so being file-backed alone is not evidence of host-local reach. Keep the logical caller unchanged. Changing the supplied readings in a separate selection control should also change a feasible winner; neither exercise claims measured economics or permits migration of existing state."),
    h2(text: "4. Existing authorities and the missing connections"),
    p(text: "This program's subject is the logical consumer's common authoring surface across reads, writes and computations. Environmental readiness is one completion route it consumes; selection and immutable-result reuse retain their own authorities. That broader consumer scope is why its single governance row is at the compiler architecture, rather than assigning the whole program to the environmental specialization."),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "std.fabric_storage is the storage interface: FabricObject, FabricHeadExpectation, FabricPut, FabricHeadRead, FabricHeadAdvance and FabricClosureRead already compose immutable objects and conditional named heads. gunbc.fabric.fabric_storage_client exposes fabric_storage_put, fabric_storage_head, fabric_storage_advance and fabric_storage_closure over FabricStorageBinding. Use these authorities rather than adding a logical-storage interface beside them."),
      li(text: "gunbc.fabric.fabric_storage_file_store implements files; gunbc.fabric.fabric_object_r2 provides put_fabric_object_r2 and get_fabric_object_r2; gunbc.fabric.fabric_storage_r2_head provides r2_head_read and r2_head_advance. R2 is not yet an arm of FabricStorageBinding. Composing those existing operations behind the shared binding is fabric work, including object-before-head publication, closure reads, CAS admission and uncertain-write outcomes. The pilot does not require new backend implementations or production cost instruments."),
      li(text: "gunbc.fabric.fabric_storage_placement and fabric_storage_binding own current placement/access routing. Production file-store clients reach the admitted door/socket or HTTPS route. FabricStorageLocalFiles is the serving implementation or an injected fixture, not permission for a consumer to bypass that admission because its configured cost is zero."),
      li(text: "std.decision::select_realization and std.pareto own candidate constraints, evidence and selection. SelectionReceipt identifies the scoped choice. The profile above projects into those models rather than introducing another decision algebra."),
      li(text: "gunbc.ensure and gunbc.owned_directory::owned_directory_ensure already support real consumers and observe/decide/apply/readback behavior. std.realization_reconcile::ConvergedEffect classifies supplied reports; by itself it does not establish that the selected effect actually ran or produced the observation."),
      li(text: "std.materialization_ladder and std.materialization_provider own reuse of admitted immutable results. The ladder explicitly excludes mutable keyed state. Extending the common authoring experience must preserve that distinction."),
      li(text: "gunbc.plans.v2_compiler_architecture owns completion and residuals; gunbc.plans.ensure_closure_design owns the environmental specialization. Omitted-operand completion is a target, not a capability supplied by this proposal. Today's dashboard_instance_directories::dashboard_instance_directory_demands remains authored."),
      li(text: "gunbc.auth.authorization_pattern_selection::select_authorization_pattern selects an existing authorization mechanism; privileged_effect_census describes coverage. A constructor cannot confer an authority the deployment does not possess."),
    ]),
    p(text: "The first decisive join is selection to effect: admission, actuation with uncertain completion, and independent observation of the receipt's selected realization. DESIGN section 3d identifies the effectful cycle as lacking a consumed shared home. The pilot must consume or help establish that contract with the owning convergence/admission work, not mint a competing cycle. A changed subject, candidate field, constraints, policy or evidence invalidates the old selection. The operation must receive a result constructed through the actual selected route and readback, not a success flag beside an independently chosen path."),
    p(text: "The second join is consumer demand to prerequisites. For the bounded pilot, model the necessary facts at the owning interface before changing callers and derive setup/use from the same values. A second handwritten store registry is not completion. General inference belongs to the existing compiler and demand-engine plans; wiring one known route does not establish universal closure."),
    p(text: "The third join is a useful diagnostic. Existing domains have typed refusal outcomes; this proposal does not declare that a generic residual carrier already exists. At the pilot boundary, WorktreeClaimNotRecorded currently carries detail: String, flattening distinct causes such as lost race and readback mismatch. The domain migration identifies the existing lower-level reasons and their owners so the outcome can preserve them instead of inventing a parallel taxonomy. A missing derivation carries the dependency path and the authority that can answer it. A closed operation's I/O refusal or contention remains its runtime outcome."),
    h2(text: "5. First worked behavior: worktree claims"),
    p(text: "A worktree is a Git checkout. The worktree-claims directory stores ownership records; it is not the checkout itself. gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_worktree_claim::worktree_claim_record_before_add writes a create-only claim and verifies it before git worktree add. Its settlement path uses cas_slot_keys to enumerate records. The motivating classes are gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_store_root_nothing_creates and gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.an_attempt_worktree_has_no_owner_until_the_attempt_state_exists."),
    p(text: "The existing root declaration, roadmap_attempt_worktree_claim_root::worktree_claim_slots_directory, already derives path and owner from HostDashboardInstance and declares DirectoryOwnerOnly. Deployment separately enrolls it; runtime independently passes the root. The migration moves storage responsibility into fabric's existing contract and setup route, preserving the domain's behavior while removing consumer-owned directory enrollment and raw-root plumbing."),
    p(text: "The record operation already calls worktree_claim_open, reads through worktree_claim_read, and compares claim identity and worktree path. Preserve that executed readback as the baseline; the missing selection-to-effect connection is above it. Keep the existing attempt lifecycle, publication, retention and recovery semantics. Trace worktree_claim_open through gunbc.compute.attempt_lifecycle::attempt_open_payload and its file_compare_and_set route before selecting a replacement; do not substitute the windowed/head-only API merely because it also offers conditional update. The fabric candidate must additionally establish enumeration, retention, consistency scope and authority continuity before it can serve this whole behavior."),
    p(text: "The R2 head's conditional publication already has a declaration: fabric_storage_r2_head::r2_head_advance_plan uses PutIfAbsent or PutIfMatch, and r2_head_fabric_advance requires R2HeadCasAdmitted. Preserve that admission; low example cost cannot supply it. FabricClosureRead follows links from a known head and is not enumeration of all claim keys. Recovery therefore needs a fabric-owned representation/operation that preserves today's cas_slot_keys behavior. That is a claim-migration obligation, separate from exercising object storage selection on both existing backends."),
    CodeBlock { code: "logical claim operation\n  -> existing domain contract\n  -> std.fabric_storage operations\n  -> fabric-owned file/R2 selection and SelectionReceipt\n  -> selected backend's access, setup, admission and readback\n  -> domain result through the selected binding\n\nExample unresolved path:\nrecord claim -> fabric storage -> selected backend -> consumer access\nOwner to answer: deployment/access authority" },
    h2(text: "6. Three bounded deliveries"),
    ol(items: [
      li(text: "Fabric interface and two-backend example. Reuse std.fabric_storage and its file/R2 operations; complete the necessary shared binding and fabric-owned selection with supplied 0/0 versus 1/1 example inputs. Start with object put/readback on isolated resources, showing the smallest caller and its inherited policy. Execute local and R2 through that same interface in the two contexts above. No production metering project is required to start."),
      li(text: "One complete domain consumer. Enumerate claim record, read, conditional-update and settlement callers; map their requirements to fabric's existing models and name any missing recovery operation. Land missing contracts before migrating. Connect selection, prerequisites, actual admission, execution and readback across recording and settlement plus both deployment routes. Preserve existing publication, retention and recovery. Keep necessary platform binding at the fabric/deployment root, consumed by both setup and use; delete independent consumer setup enrollment."),
      li(text: "Adoption and refinement. Prove the migrated logical caller unchanged in a second isolated deployment, with unsupported domain operations excluded before backend ranking. Exercise the shared interface on both backends for their admitted operations. Add calibrated or metered inputs later through the same fabric policy and receipt, without changing consumers. The pilot does not require live migration, every provider, general prerequisite inference or completion of the whole compiler."),
    ]),
    p(text: "Use the remaining explicit wiring from these deliveries to identify the next small completion obligation in the existing compiler program. Credential-acquisition and session-placement stores are subsequent comparison cases, not prerequisites for finishing the first example. Approval consolidation is a separate follow-up: sensitivity in context and one route for the formal approvals that remain."),
    h2(text: "7. Evidence and conformance review"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "Start the real-path witness with only the parent directory. Derive/provision the child under the admitted authority and perform the actual record/read/enumeration route as the consumer principal. Repeat directory/setup reconciliation to establish Noop; a duplicate claim write must retain its existing lost-race/refusal behavior. Preserve a real producer-path witness alongside inexpensive supplied-boundary tests."),
      li(text: "Delete prerequisite production and require the migrated operation to fail before a successful claim write or checkout launch. Wrong instance, foreign ownership, inaccessible state and failed readback must not produce a usable store. State whether each protection is model construction, compile-time admission or runtime refusal."),
      li(text: "The explicit local 0/0 and R2 positive example selects local when both are admissible; a second context that excludes local selects R2 and performs its real put/readback. A supplied-input control changes the feasible winner when readings change. The receipts retain example standing. A required performance floor without admissible evidence returns SelectionNeedsEvidence; synthetic predictions do not satisfy it. An absent optional SLO creates no promise."),
      li(text: "Changing a selection input invalidates its receipt. A post-actuation response cannot retroactively prove that admission happened before the effect. Model ordering at the effectful construction boundary and observe uncertain completion before retry according to the existing recovery law."),
      li(text: "An unavailable authoritative store must not be interpreted as absence or trigger a fresh fallback store. Equivalent behavior and refusal semantics, not merely the same method signatures, establish provider compatibility."),
      li(text: "Review asks what the author still supplies, why the shared model cannot derive it, and what integration points disappeared. Recognizing a competing representation remains a judgment. Do not add a universal conformance checker or a test that only asserts the new declaration exists."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "8. Open implementation questions"),
    ol(items: [
      li(text: "Where should fabric's existing placement/binding policy carry the initial configured readings and inherited service requirements? Reuse existing decision, measure and evidence-standing carriers. The two policy concepts above do not justify a new generic profile or storage authority."),
      li(text: "What is the owning consumed contract for SelectionReceipt -> admission -> actuation -> independent observation? Coordinate with the convergence/admission lane before implementation. The deployment-gate stage-2 proposal [gunbc#14757](https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/pull/14757) is a concrete domain example of phase construction: each phase produces the confined input required by the next, and the effect response is bound to the request it answers. It is an alignment reference, not the shared home or evidence that this pilot is implemented."),
      li(text: "What fabric-owned enumeration or index operation preserves worktree recovery, and how do R2 object/head/closure operations compose behind FabricStorageBinding? Resolve those contracts in their current homes. Keep the object put/readback example moving while the full domain migration is specified."),
      li(text: "Which remaining explicit dependency can the current compiler derive next without a new syntax or wrapper around an unresolved model deficit? The pilot supplies the concrete input to that decision."),
    ]),
  ]
}

data logical_work_realization_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly { ruling: project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts },
  slug: "logical-work-realization",
  title: "Logical work realization: a small SLO and arbitration interface",
  body: logical_work_realization_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Retire this proposal when fabric-owned selection executes both file and R2 backends through the shared storage interface with explicit example-standing controls, recording and settlement consume the same grounded fabric binding, feature callers no longer author infrastructure arguments or independent setup enrollment, both provisioning routes consume the same requirements, and the unchanged logical caller works in a second isolated deployment. The owning domain models must carry the policy, selection-to-effect connection and executed controls. Any remaining authored root binding is named and justified. Production metering is a refinement of those inputs, not a retirement prerequisite; remaining general compiler-completion obligations are recorded in the existing implementation program. Those consumed contracts and evidence then own the facts this proposal discusses.") },
}
